WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Kiev is negotiating to lift starshields 160 km per hour caps that slow drone intercepts. This

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.200
is SpaceX Daily, episode 134. Ukrainian presidential adviser Sergei Beskresnov told Envy that Kiev

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.360
is talking with SpaceX, the Pentagon, and the US government after the limits appeared without

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.380
warning early Thursday morning. The new settings disconnect terminals and have four slower

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.740
flight profiles that leave drones and helicopters more exposed to Russian air defenses. Those

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.400
Those slower profiles also give Russian aerial targets more chances to evade interception.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.360
Bess Krasnov said Star Shield controls interceptor drones chasing Russian jet-powered drones and

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.660
supports helicopters hunting shahead drones.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.740
He said the system is not used on Russian territory or for strikes on oil refineries.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.540
The change appears tied to political factors beyond technical or commercial issues.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:58.313
U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington is considering Ukraine's request for

00:00:58.313 --> 00:01:02.253
star-shield access to support long-range strikes inside Russian territory.

00:01:02.873 --> 00:01:07.353
Rubio clarified that star-shield remains separate from commercial star-link and operates

00:01:07.353 --> 00:01:09.153
under a direct Pentagon contract.

00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:13.273
He said the military system is not available to Ukraine at this moment.

00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:17.473
He called reports of a deliberate U.S. disruption categorically false.

00:01:18.093 --> 00:01:22.893
Service performance had returned to prior levels without any White House order to reduce speeds.

00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:28.053
President Trump also denied ordering any temporary disruption of star-link services for

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:28.993
Ukraine's military.

00:01:29.713 --> 00:01:33.333
Discussions continue on how Kiev would want to use the military system.

00:01:34.212 --> 00:01:38.092
Florida is the launch site for Falcon 9's Bandwagon 5 ride share.

00:01:38.732 --> 00:01:43.932
SpaceX said teams encapsulated 32 customer spacecraft in the standard pre-launch step

00:01:43.932 --> 00:01:45.952
that keeps the manifest on schedule.

00:01:46.977 --> 00:01:52.517
A SpaceX Dragon spacecraft docked with the International Space Station, CW-39 reports.

00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:56.857
The capsule delivered organoids and equipment for artificial retina research.

00:01:56.857 --> 00:02:00.817
science operations and microgravity continue without interruption.

00:02:01.874 --> 00:02:07.494
Frank Rimmer-Man Advisors, Steel Peak Wealth, Gemmer Asset Management, and IFP Advisors

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.254
each filed new SPCX share acquisitions.

00:02:10.714 --> 00:02:14.714
The four transactions were separate institutional filings, according to Market Beat.

00:02:15.831 --> 00:02:19.791
Elon Musk posted on X that SpaceX represents an anomaly in the Matrix.

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:24.471
The line pointed at the company's place in the broader space and technology landscape.

00:02:24.471 --> 00:02:29.571
Optimus and CyberCab will form the vast majority of Tesla's value, Musk stated.

00:02:30.031 --> 00:02:35.011
He said superintelligence, robots, solar power, and mass to space are the only elements

00:02:35.011 --> 00:02:37.531
that scale economically to incredible size.

00:02:38.538 --> 00:02:44.518
Users on X link that robot and autonomy scaling to SpaceX, mass to space economics, and noted

00:02:44.518 --> 00:02:47.678
shared manufacturing and compute threads across the companies.

00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:52.638
The thread explored how first principles cost reduction in one domain could accelerate

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:53.778
progress in the others.

00:02:53.778 --> 00:02:59.061
players. The GROKBOT team is answering user feedback after recent gains in speed and

00:02:59.061 --> 00:03:04.041
intent understanding, Musk reported. The cadence is around 20 improvements per day.

00:03:04.741 --> 00:03:09.141
Worth keeping an eye on is that Ukrainian units still speculate on who had the authority

00:03:09.141 --> 00:03:10.881
to impose the Starsheel change.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:16.721
Bess Krestnov said connectivity disruptions continued afterward, possibly due to the new

00:03:16.721 --> 00:03:22.809
settings. Full flow stage combustion and raptor is today's engineering deep dive, because

00:03:22.809 --> 00:03:28.669
dumping propellant overboard is the loss this cycle refuses to accept. In a simpler gas generator

00:03:28.669 --> 00:03:34.229
engine several percent of total flow spins the turbines and then goes overboard, so that mass

00:03:34.229 --> 00:03:39.729
never makes thrust. You already pay to tank it, pump it, and carry it, and then you throw it away

00:03:39.729 --> 00:03:45.509
as warm gas. Full flow routes every kilogram of methane and every kilogram of oxygen through the

00:03:45.509 --> 00:03:50.829
pre-burners, the small combustors that drive the turbo pumps, and then into the main chamber.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:56.589
Nothing is dumped. Every kilogram is available for thrust. The closed loop raises specific

00:03:56.589 --> 00:04:01.569
impulse, which is simply how much push you get from each kilogram of propellant. It still

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:06.829
needs precise control of two separate pre-burner turbines, and it will damage hardware if mixture

00:04:06.829 --> 00:04:11.869
ratios drift. You run two pre-burners because each propellant has to spin its own pump.

00:04:12.469 --> 00:04:17.229
The methane side runs fuel-rich so the turbine gas stays cool enough not to melt the blades.

00:04:17.229 --> 00:04:25.429
The oxygen side runs ox-rich, and hot oxygen attacks metal, which is why mixture ratio control is not a nice to have.

00:04:25.969 --> 00:04:29.629
Drift too far ox-rich and you start cutting the machine you are trying to fly.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:36.409
SpaceX chose methalox, methane and liquid oxygen, over denser kerosene or toxic hypergolics,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.989
because a clean burn lets a booster fly again with little inspection.

00:04:40.709 --> 00:04:43.589
Kerosene cracks in hot cooling channels and leaves soot.

00:04:43.589 --> 00:04:49.449
Methane is one carbon to four hydrogens, so there is far less carbon to deposit, and that

00:04:49.449 --> 00:04:54.709
is the first principle's reason a methalox full-flow engine can be inspected less between flights.

00:04:55.289 --> 00:04:59.709
That choice cuts the maintenance hours that historically limited how often a first stage

00:04:59.709 --> 00:05:00.809
could return to flight.

00:05:01.529 --> 00:05:03.749
Raptor 3 then pulled the plumbing inside.

00:05:04.389 --> 00:05:10.009
External lines, flanges, and heat shield patches disappeared as turbo pump flows were internalized.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:17.449
engine mass dropped while sea level thrust lifted from the earlier 185 tons force class toward 250.

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:23.589
Each external pipe you delete is brackets, welds, insulation, and leak checks you no longer

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:30.009
carry, and leak checks you no longer perform after landing. The mass reduction compounds across 33

00:05:30.009 --> 00:05:35.969
engines on a super heavy booster, the first stage. Less engine mass lowers the propellant load needed

00:05:35.969 --> 00:05:41.749
for the same Delta V, the change in velocity the vehicle has to produce, and improves the payload

00:05:41.749 --> 00:05:47.109
fraction delivered to orbit. Losing a single chamber on that booster costs you on the order of

00:05:47.109 --> 00:05:52.969
3% of sea level thrust, which is the engine out math that lets a shutdown be a continuation rather

00:05:52.969 --> 00:05:58.869
than a failure. The same simplification shortens production time per engine, and that clock is the

00:05:58.869 --> 00:06:04.389
practical limit on how fast Starship flight rate can rise once tower catch and refueling our routine.

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:10.189
You cannot fly boosters faster than you can deliver engines, no matter how clean the catch looks.

00:06:10.849 --> 00:06:17.809
The Bessamer process in 1856 made the same move and steel by internalizing the flow and eliminating intermediate steps.

00:06:18.389 --> 00:06:27.449
The idiot index, the ratio of finished part cost to raw material cost, can collapse by an order of magnitude when the redesign hits the dominant loss mechanisms.

00:06:27.449 --> 00:06:32.869
For Raptor, the index improves from higher thrust per kilogram and from fewer post-flight

00:06:32.869 --> 00:06:37.349
inspections, which translates into more flights per booster before refurbishment.

00:06:37.949 --> 00:06:42.809
Raw metal and propellant are cheap compared with an engine you can only use once, or an

00:06:42.809 --> 00:06:44.869
engine you have to tear down after every hop.

00:06:45.549 --> 00:06:50.729
The cycle also supports the airline-level reliability target SpaceX has set for point-to-point

00:06:50.729 --> 00:06:55.729
Earth transport, where engine out-tolerance and rapid turnaround are first-order requirements

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:57.189
resistance rather than afterthoughts.

